// F2 prerequisite (2026-09-09): T122 rejects a fn named like a BUILTIN, not just
// like a keyword -- but its hash table was short by seven of the 36 builtins
// emit_call_or_ctor dispatches, and `clz` was one of them. Before the fix this
// file compiled rc=0 and `clz(8)` returned 60: the builtin ladder runs BEFORE the
// user-fn lookup, so the user's `clz` became silent dead code and the 5 was never
// reachable. That is the failure this construct exists to keep dead -- a
// mechanism with no negative construct is one refactor from vanishing.
// EXPECT COMPILEFAIL:99 from: function named like builtin (F2)
fn clz(x: i64) -> i64 { 5 }
fn main() -> i64 { clz(8) }
